              "`ChartSlotView` is `ReactNode | ComponentType`: every slot — the reading's view, the span's, an annotation's — takes a component as well as an element, and a component is rendered with no props of its own. That is what puts the app's own views in a `zyplot` config. An element is a new value on every render, so a config holding one is rebuilt on every render with it; a component reference is the same value for the life of the module, so the config is too. What the view shows comes from its own hooks rather than from a prop threaded through the chart, which means a reading changes the chip and nothing else: the chart's props are untouched, `memo` holds, and on iOS and Android the dataset is not serialised again for a finger that moved.",
